# =====================================================================================
# resolution_lane_twoop.ttl — the TWO-OPERATION V7 provenance-closure lane (W2 · SP0 · Stage 3a
# CONSOLIDATION, T-PROV-2OP). The two-operation companion of reviews/resolved/resolution_lane.ttl +
# reviews/executor/executor_lane.ttl + reviews/shadow/shadow_lane.ttl (the committed one-operation lane).
# =====================================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Gate V7 (design §4; run-algebra-checks.sh:435-470) requires EVERY reshaped record
# (every subject bearing @rel:authority) to be attributed to >= 1 EXECUTOR agent AND >= 1 SHADOW agent
# (prov:wasAttributedTo) plus a prov:wasGeneratedBy. The committed one-operation lane closes this for the
# 29 one-op reshaped records (magma..abelian_group). The five NEW two-operation rungs (T-RING + the
# semiring/field/module/vector_space siblings) minted the D24 provenance QUARTET (@rel:authority "SYN" +
# @rel:created/modified/version/state) on their 28 reshaped records — 5 model-records + 5 theory-records +
# 13 reduct/connecting/morphism records + 5 theorem-records — but did NOT author the V7 dual-attribution
# lane, so the full runner was V7 RED on exactly those 28 records (and only those). This file is the
# Stage-3a CONSOLIDATION closure of that lane — the direct analogue of re-deriving spine.yaml for V6.
#
# WHY A NEW FILE (additive). The three committed one-op lane files (resolution_lane.ttl / executor_lane.ttl
# / shadow_lane.ttl) are committed atoms; per the Stage-3a scope lock the consolidation ONLY ADDS files
# under basicttl/primordial/type/algebra/**. So the two-op closure is a single new additive file that
# folds the resolution (scope marker + wasGeneratedBy) AND the executor + shadow attribution edges into
# one place for the 28 two-op records. It REUSES by IRI (bridge-never-duplicate) the scope-marker class,
# the Draft activity and the executor/shadow agents already defined in the committed lane files — it mints
# no new provenance vocabulary.
#
# HONESTY (Praeriehund; §7.2). The generic SP0-spine-fold executor + shadow agents are the SAME whole-fold
# agents the 29 one-op records use; attributing the 28 two-op records to them is TRUTHFUL at the granularity
# this provenance layer operates: each two-op rung genuinely ran as an operator-loop executor exec WITH a
# tandem shadow verdict (the Stage-3a fan-out: T-2OP-INFRA/T-RING + 4 siblings, each with shadow "PASS"),
# and each record was drafted by the SP0 spine-fold Draft activity. This is faithful replication of the
# committed one-op pattern, NOT fabricated attribution. RESIDUAL for the maintainer sign-off packet: the
# rung executors OMITTED their own V7 lane; the consolidation closed it here. If the maintainer wants
# per-rung executor/shadow agent granularity (distinct agents per rung) rather than the whole-fold generic
# agents, that is a §7.2 sign-off refinement — the one-op tower itself uses the generic agents, so this
# lane matches the established precedent.
#
# Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-w2-sp0-primordial-fold-design.md (§4 V7).
# Consumes (do not rewrite): reviews/resolved/resolution_lane.ttl (scope-marker class + Draft activity),
# reviews/executor/executor_lane.ttl (executor agent), reviews/shadow/shadow_lane.ttl (shadow agent).
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .

# --- scope marker + generation + dual attribution on every two-op reshaped record ---
